    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/keira-dynasty">Keira</a> sultans ruled Darfur from Jebel Marra for over 250 years, building an Islamic state in the eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sahel">Sahel</a>.</li><li>Its Forty Days Road carried slaves, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ivory-trade">ivory</a> and feathers to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a>, and West African pilgrims passed through it to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mecca">Mecca</a>.</li><li>Conquered in 1874 and revived in 1898, it fell to an Anglo-Egyptian force with aircraft in 1916.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>Much of what we know of the sultanate's court comes from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muhammad-al-tunisi">Muhammad al-Tunisi</a>, a Tunisian traveller who lived in Darfur from about 1803 to 1811.</p></aside>
    </section>

